{# Managed by ansible-supply-chain-security.
   Tier auto-selected from detected Composer version.
     Composer ≥ 2.9   : full audit block (block-insecure + block-abandoned + abandoned)
     Composer 2.7-2.8 : audit block with abandoned only
     Composer < 2.7   : no audit block (key added in 2.7.0)
     Composer not detected at apply time: rendered as < 2.7 (safe baseline);
       re-run the role after installing Composer to upgrade to the matching tier.

   allow-plugins is NOT tiered. When denying we always emit `{}`.
     MEASURED (composer 2.0.14 → 2.10.3, 16 phars): `"allow-plugins": false`
     is a HARD FATAL —
       PHP Fatal error: Uncaught TypeError: array_merge():
       Argument #1 must be of type array, false given
     exit 255 on install / config / dump-autoload, i.e. every command except
     --version. Ubuntu 22.04 ships composer 2.2.6, this role's oldest
     supported LTS, so the literal `false` bricked composer on every jammy
     host.
     A `>= 2.2.15` predicate looked like the fix and was NOT, because the
     upstream fix was not backported linearly:
       2.2.6 FATAL   2.2.14 FATAL   2.2.15 safe   2.2.16 safe
       2.3.0 FATAL   2.3.5 FATAL    2.3.7 FATAL   2.3.8 safe   2.4.0+ safe
     2.3.0 sorts ABOVE 2.2.15 while predating the fix, so the predicate
     emitted the bricking value across the whole 2.3.0-2.3.7 range.
     `{}` — the empty allowlist — returns rc 0 on EVERY version tested and
     still blocks every plugin, so the tier bought nothing and could only ever
     be wrong. No predicate is safer than a predicate over a non-monotonic
     property. (allow-plugins itself only exists from 2.2.0; on 2.0/2.1 the
     key is inert either way and --no-plugins in the wrapper is the layer that
     blocks plugins.)
   See README "Limitations" → "Composer audit blocking is version-tiered". #}
{%- set v = composer_detected_version | default('', true) -%}
{%- set has_audit = v != '' and v is version('2.7.0', '>=') -%}
{%- set has_block = v != '' and v is version('2.9.0', '>=') -%}
{
  "config": {
    "secure-http": true,
    "lock": true,
    "preferred-install": "dist",
    "allow-plugins": {% if composer_allow_plugins | bool %}true{% else %}{}{% endif %}{% if has_audit %},
    "audit": {
      "abandoned": "{{ composer_audit_abandoned }}"{% if has_block %},
      "block-insecure": {{ composer_audit_block_insecure | bool | lower }},
      "block-abandoned": {{ composer_audit_block_abandoned | bool | lower }}{% endif %}
    }{% endif %}
  }
}
